<title>JAPAN: Japan July construction orders up 1.7%.</title>
<headline>Japan July construction orders up 1.7%.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's construction orders in July rose 1.7 percent from a year earlier to 1.45 trillion yen, the Construction Ministry said on Friday (in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p> Domestic private sector orders		943.96  +14.7</p>
<p> Domestic public sector orders		 403.10  -23.1</p>
<p>Foreign government facilities in Japan</p>
<p>   and orders of less than 10 million yen   55.29  +48.8</p>
<p> Orders received abroad			   46.83  +14.2</p>
<p> Total						1.45 trln +1.7</p>
</text>
